$ cessna210_flagship_massset.bdf — SOL 144 payload sweep driver (Step 65)
$
$ One airframe, one flight condition (TRIM 1: 1g, q = 2334 Pa), three payload
$ conditions selected per subcase with the case-control MASSSET request:
$
$   SUBCASE 1  MASSSET 10  FERRY    996.0 kg  baseline less rear-seat payload
$   SUBCASE 2  MASSSET 20  CRUISE  1201.0 kg  + 120 kg half wing fuel
$   SUBCASE 3  MASSSET 30  MTOW    1560.0 kg  + 240 kg full wing fuel
$                                             + rear-seat payload 85 -> 324 kg
$
$ The AIC, splines, stiffness and the whole AeroCache are geometry/Mach-only
$ and are built ONCE and shared; only the mass-derived operators (M_gg, M_ax,
$ GPWG, the trim solve) are rebuilt per case.
$
$ Two things to read out of the .f06:
$   1. ANGLEA rises monotonically FERRY -> CRUISE -> MTOW: more weight needs
$      more lift needs more incidence at fixed q.
$   2. The MWROOT wing-root bending PER UNIT AIRCRAFT WEIGHT FALLS as fuel
$      goes into the wing.  That is inertia relief: wing fuel sits outboard of
$      the root cut, so its weight cancels part of the lift there.  It is the
$      reason a loads engineer certifies the zero-fuel case, not the MTOW one.
$
$ Walk-through: docs/20_theory/02_realistic_airplane_sol144.md
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa, s)
$
SOL 144
TITLE = Cessna 210 flagship — payload / mass-case sweep at 1g
INCLUDE 'cessna210_flagship_bulk.bdf'
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE   = FERRY
  TRIM    = 1
  SPC     = 1
  MASSSET = 10
$
SUBCASE 2
  TITLE   = CRUISE
  TRIM    = 1
  SPC     = 1
  MASSSET = 20
$
SUBCASE 3
  TITLE   = MTOW
  TRIM    = 1
  SPC     = 1
  MASSSET = 30
$
BEGIN BULK
ENDDATA
